WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:07.554
CompTIA Network Plus, domain 4, Network security, which is 14 percent of the exam.

00:00:07.554 --> 00:00:10.196
This lesson covers objective 4 point 3.

00:00:10.196 --> 00:00:15.953
Given a scenario, apply network security features, defense techniques, and solutions.

00:00:15.953 --> 00:00:20.830
Today's concept: the order in which an access control list is evaluated.

00:00:23.170 --> 00:00:26.170
An access control list is a numbered set of rules.

00:00:26.170 --> 00:00:28.570
The device reads them from the top down.

00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:32.168
A packet from host ten dot one dot one dot five arrives.

00:00:32.168 --> 00:00:34.210
It is compared with rule one first.

00:00:34.530 --> 00:00:36.646
It matches rule one, so it is denied.

00:00:36.646 --> 00:00:40.020
The first match wins, and rule two is never even looked at.

00:00:41.370 --> 00:00:42.894
That is why order matters.

00:00:42.894 --> 00:00:48.580
If the broad permit were first, host five would be allowed through, and the deny would never run.

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:53.211
If a packet matches no rule at all, it falls off the end.

00:00:53.211 --> 00:00:57.160
Every list finishes with an implicit deny, so the packet is dropped.

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:06.633
For the exam, an access control list is read from the top down, and the first rule that matches decides.

00:01:06.633 --> 00:01:10.525
If nothing matches, the implicit deny at the end drops the packet.

00:01:10.525 --> 00:01:12.530
That's objective four point three.
